#macro ChoiceStatCheck(statName, statValue) \
    $data   CheckStat = "$statName" \
    $data   CheckStatValue = $statValue
#macro ChoiceTime(time) \
    $data   TIme = $time

#basePath TestChapter

// #region Opening

:: Start
@trigger    ChapterStart
@cutscene

$call SetBackground("bg/Nightmare.png")

{@}     They're late.
        Those two asked you to meet and they're <i>late</i>.
        At least, you think they're late.
$choice .Start.Late.A; Who?
$choice .Start.Late.B; I think?
$choose branch
{@}     Might as well pass the time until they arrive.

$choice .Start.Bench; Sit on the bench.
$choice .Start.Railing; Lean over the railing.
$choose branch

{@}     ...
        Why did you come to this town?
$choice .Start.Arrival.A; To investigate
$choice .Start.Arrival.B; To escape
$choice .Start.Arrival.C; I don't remember.
$choose branch

{@}     ...
        Okay, they're officially too late.
        The anglers might have just... forgotten about you.
        That's fine. You can still enjoy the sights.
$choice .Start.EndOfDock; Walk to the end of the dock.
$choose branch

$goto .WakeUp

:: Start.Late.A
{@}     The anglers.
        They said they had "something important to show you."
        And it had to be in person, for whatever reason.

:: Start.Late.B
{@}     You could be wrong.
        You've been known to forget things from time to time.
        But you're pretty sure the anglers were supposed to be here by now.

:: Start.Bench
{@}     You park yourself on a nearby bench.
        The boards creak softly in response.

:: Start.Railing
{@}     You lean your weight on the railing.
        Some rust flakes off on your skin.
        
:: Start.Arrival.A
$set local:dream.arrival.reason = "investigate"
{@}     That's right.
        You were sent to look into...
$choice .Start.Arrival.A.Fish; Fish populations
$choice .Start.Arrival.A.Food; Local restaurants
$choice .Start.Arrival.A.Joke; A murder! Ooh spooky

:: Start.Arrival.A.Fish
$set local:dream.fish = true
{@}     Fish populations.
        They were trending downward, if I recall.
        You are an... ecologist.
$call AdjustStat(Research, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.A.Food
$set local:dream.restaurant = true
{@}     Local restaurants.
        There's an up-and-coming poutine place downtown.
        You are a... famous food critic. Sure.
$call AdjustStat(Innovate, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.A.Joke
$set local:dream.crows = true
{@}     A... murder.
        Not sure what crows have to do with this, but okay.
        You are an... ornithologist. Fine.
$call AdjustStat(Communicate, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.B
$set local:dream.arrival.reason = "escape"
{@}     That's right.
        You wanted to escape from...
$choice .Start.Arrival.B.Job; A dead-end job
$choice .Start.Arrival.B.Brooding; Myself (oh so brooding)
$choice .Start.Arrival.B.Joke; ...A giant trout?

:: Start.Arrival.B.Job
$set local:dream.broke = true
{@}     A dead-end job.
        A living wage was out-of-reach there, and rent just kept climbing.
        You hope... to make rent out here.
$call AdjustStat(Ranger, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.B.Brooding
$set local:dream.brooding = true
{@}     ...Yourself.
        A little on-the-nose I think.
        But sure I can roll with that.
$call AdjustStat(Communicate, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.B.Joke
$set local:dream.trout = true
{@}     A... giant trout?
        ...What?
        Okay fine a giant trout was chasing you and you fled heroically.
$call AdjustStat(Tech, 1)

:: Start.Arrival.C
$set level:dream.arrival.reason = "unknown"
{@}     You don't remember.
        How curious.

:: Start.EndOfDock
{@}     You see yourself in the murky water.

$choice .Start.EndOfDock.A; She stares back.
$choice .Start.EndOfDock.B; They stare back.
$choice .Start.EndOfDock.C; He stares back.
$choose branch

{@}     {pg His|Her|Their} face suddenly sinks beneath the waves.
        Your heart follows suit and crashes to your stomach.
        The stench of rotting fish wafts up. You suppress the urge to gag.
        The surface of the water begins to writhe and contort.

:: Start.EndOfDock.A
$set global:gender="f"

:: Start.EndOfDock.B
$set global:gender="x"

:: Start.EndOfDock.C
$set global:gender="m"

// #endregion

// #region Bedroom

:: WakeUp
@cutscene

$call ClearVisibleLines()
$call SetBackground("bg/Room.png")
{@}     Reality arrives swiftly and disorientingly.
{@Player}   Ugh, haven't had one of those in ages.{auto}
$if local:dream.restaurant
            I could really go for some fries right now...
$elseif local:dream.crows
            And what was that about birds...
$elseif local:dream.fish
            Upcoming job's really got me stressed out...
$elseif local:dream.broke
            Finances haven't been that tight, right?
$elseif local:dream.brooding
            Thought I was over that by now...
$elseif local:dream.trout
            Utter nonsense...
$else
            So strange...
$endif
{@Player}   Welp, another one for my therapist.

{@}     On your desk, you spot several notes you've taken.

$call GiveEvidenceCard("Evidence-Lamprey-Discovered")

$goto .Finishing

// #endregion

:: Finishing

$call BeginIntervention()